03:42.330 --> 03:44.700
which actually, it's confusing,

03:44.700 --> 03:46.800
it doesn't have anything to do with this really,

03:46.800 --> 03:50.637
dash L is telling it to list all the tags

03:50.637 --> 03:53.760
which we don't have to do here, right?

03:53.760 --> 03:54.870
We just get them all.

03:54.870 --> 03:58.230
But if I add the dash L, it's implicit

03:58.230 --> 04:01.980
when I do git tag, we're actually doing dash L,

04:01.980 --> 04:04.200
just we're saying list all the tags.

04:04.200 --> 04:06.867
But when we try and filter with some

04:06.867 --> 04:09.420
some sort of wild card like we have here

04:09.420 --> 04:11.850
this is a pattern that we're trying to match.

04:11.850 --> 04:13.410
So that star inside the quotes

04:13.410 --> 04:16.290
an asterisk here means any character

04:16.290 --> 04:19.830
this is going to find all tags that contain beta in them

04:19.830 --> 04:23.340
and we have to use dash L in order to list them out.

04:23.340 --> 04:25.708
It's kind of weird, but that's just how it works.

04:25.708 --> 04:30.000
So as an example, if I wanted to look at all the,

04:30.000 --> 04:33.360
